  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Max bursts into the delivery room without shoe covers expecting to see Vika, only to find another patient named Goncharova. When he finally reaches Vika by phone, she surprises him.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Эй, наденьте бахилы немедленно!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вика, это ты здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Нет, меня зовут Маша.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Подождите, а где Гончарова?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Я тоже Гончарова.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где другая Гончарова?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Ребёнок никак рождаться не хочет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, Вика, а ты где?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Я сейчас на работе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты разве ещё не рожаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Нет, я очень занята.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас приеду в отель.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Эй, наденьте бахилы немедленно!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hey, put on shoe covers immediately!' The grammar packs 'hey' and 'immediately' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вика, это ты здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vika, is that you here?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Vika' before landing on 'here'. the doctor answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Нет, меня зовут Маша.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, my name is Masha.' the doctor brings out the contrast between 'no' and 'me' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Подождите, а где Гончарова?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, where is Goncharova?' The meaning hinges on 'wait' working together with 'Goncharova' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Я тоже Гончарова.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Goncharova too.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'Goncharova' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где другая Гончарова?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where is the other Goncharova?' Max brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'where' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "doctor",
      "t": "Ребёнок никак рождаться не хочет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The baby just does not want to be born yet.' Notice how Russian expresses 'child' and 'wants' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, Вика, а ты где?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, Vika, where are you?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'hello' before landing on 'where'. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Я сейчас на работе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am at work right now.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'work' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты разве ещё не рожаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you not giving birth yet?' Max raises the pitch on 'to give birth' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Нет, я очень занята.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I am very busy.' Vika brings out the contrast between 'no' and 'I' in a few short words. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас приеду в отель.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am coming to the hotel right now.' Max anchors the line on 'I', while 'hotel' completes the thought. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
